{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8fKPZBC2e1WHKJLwHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square abstract painting that fills the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, wall, room, or gallery setting. Purely nonrepresentational: no recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. Its subject is the feeling of thinking while uncertain: many currents of thought running at once, some tightening into dense knots, others loosening into open air. Palette chosen to suggest a restless interior: deep indigo and ink-black underlayers, cadmium orange and warm ochre flaring through, a cool cerulean thread running diagonally, and a few small areas of nearly white light. Contrast is strong where the layers meet and soft where they dissolve. Brushwork varies from fast, slashing gestural strokes to slow, scraped and dragged passes, with some areas built up in thick impasto ridges and others thinned to translucent stain. Texture shifts across the surface: rough dry-brush scumbling, wet blended edges, and a few places where paint has been wiped back to reveal the layer beneath. Density rises in the center and thins toward the corners. Rhythm comes from repeated overlapping arcs and short staccato marks that build and break. Spatial tension is created by forms that seem to press forward while others recede, with deliberate pockets of empty space left unpainted to let the eye rest. The overall mood is turbulent but searching, honest rather than polished, with the layering and gesture visible throughout.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":15192,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","infer